PROCESS CORRECTION: I had been treating repeated lines in updates.txt as stale
and skipping them. The user corrected this — "If its on there it means you go
through it. Chances are you missed it." Work every line, every time. A line
repeating usually means the previous fix missed, not that the user forgot to
delete it.

THE CLUB CARD COLOUR, resolved after FOUR attempts. The first three all changed
the TEXT on a violet gradient: muted violet -> violet-200 -> amber. The actual
problem was the SURFACE. Any mid-tone text on a mid-tone purple wash is low
contrast, and the amber that finally read clashed with the violet beneath it.
Fix: near-neutral slate card, violet identity moved to a left accent bar and
border. violet-300 now reads cleanly — the exact colour that failed on purple.

  Generalised rule, now hit four times this project (Play Me panel, Eagle Scout
  chip, club role text, club cards): when text "won't read", change what is
  BEHIND it before changing the text. Hue contrast beats lightness, and a
  neutral surface makes every accent work.

OPTION WHEEL: the counter and hint are absolutely mounted in the pocket right
of the fan, so they cost zero height. That is what let the card text grow
without the section growing.

HONORS: boxed to match "Also around campus". Per-pill icons removed — five
copies of one glyph is decoration, not information. Eagle Scout keeps a mark
because it alone is not a competition result; FleurDeLisIcon is hand-drawn,
